### B. THEORY ABOUT INTERVAL-VALUED INTUITIONISTIC FUZZY SET

*Definition 1 [41]:* Let X be a nonempty set, and then the interval-valued intuitionistic fuzzy set (IVIFS) is defined as

$$A = \left\{ x, \left( \left[ \mu_A^L(x), \mu_A^H(x) \right], \left[ \nu_A^L(x), \nu_A^H(x) \right] \right) \middle| x \in X \right\}$$
(1)

where$$\mu_A^L(x)$$ and $$\mu_A^H(x)$$ represent the upper and lower bounds of the membership degree, respectively, and $$\mu_A^L(x), \mu_A^H(x) \subseteq [0, 1]$$. $$\nu_A^L(x)$$ and $$\nu_A^H(x)$$ represent the upper and lower bounds of the nonmembership degree, respectively, $$\nu_A^L(x), \nu_A^H(x) \subseteq [0, 1]$$, and $$\mu_A^H(x) + \nu_A^H(x) \leq 1$$. $$\pi_A^L(x)$$ and $$\pi_A^H(x)$$ represent the upper and lower bounds of the hesitation degree, respectively, $$\pi_A^L(x) = 1 - \mu_A^H(x) - \nu_A^H(x)$$, $$\pi_A^H(x) = 1 - \mu_A^L(x) - \nu_A^L(x)$$.

The IVIFN $$\left( \left[ \mu_A^L(x), \mu_A^H(x) \right], \left[ \nu_A^L(x), \nu_A^H(x) \right] \right)$$ is expressed as $$\left( \left[ \mu_A^L, \mu_A^H \right], \left[ \nu_A^L, \nu_A^H \right] \right)$$ for convenience.

*Definition 2 [42], [43]:* Let $$\alpha_1 = \left( \left[ \mu_1^L, \mu_1^H \right], \left[ \nu_1^L, \nu_1^H \right] \right)$$ and $$\alpha_2 = \left( \left[ \mu_2^L, \mu_2^H \right], \left[ \nu_2^L, \nu_2^H \right] \right)$$ be any two IVIFNs, then the operations of IVIFNs are defined as

$$\alpha_1 \oplus \alpha_2 = \left( \left[ 1 - \left( 1 - \mu_1^L \right) \left( 1 - \mu_2^L \right), 1 - \left( 1 - \mu_1^H \right) \left( 1 - \mu_2^H \right) \right], \left[ \nu_1^L \times \nu_2^L, \nu_1^H \times \nu_2^H \right] \right);$$

$$\alpha_1 \otimes \alpha_2 = \left( \left[ \mu_1^L \times \mu_2^L, \mu_1^H \times \mu_2^H \right], \left[ 1 - \left( 1 - \nu_1^L \right) \left( 1 - \nu_2^L \right), 1 - \left( 1 - \nu_1^H \right) \left( 1 - \nu_2^H \right) \right] \right);$$

$$\alpha_1 \cap \alpha_2 = \left( \left[ \min \left( \mu_1^L, \mu_2^L \right), \min \left( \mu_1^H, \mu_2^H \right) \right], \left[ \max \left( \nu_1^L, \nu_2^L \right), \max \left( \nu_1^H, \nu_2^H \right) \right] \right);$$$$\alpha_1 \cup \alpha_2 = \left( \left[ \max \left( \mu_1^L, \mu_2^L \right), \max \left( \mu_1^H, \mu_2^H \right) \right], \left[ \min \left( \nu_1^L, \nu_2^L \right), \min \left( \nu_1^H, \nu_2^H \right) \right] \right);$$

$$\lambda \alpha_1 = \left( \left[ 1 - \left( 1 - \mu_1^L \right)^\lambda, 1 - \left( 1 - \mu_1^H \right)^\lambda \right], \left[ \left( \nu_1^L \right)^\lambda, \left( \nu_1^H \right)^\lambda \right] \right), \lambda > 0;$$

$$\alpha_1^\lambda = \left( \left[ \left( \mu_1^L \right)^\lambda, \left( \mu_1^H \right)^\lambda \right], \left[ 1 - \left( 1 - \nu_1^L \right)^\lambda, 1 - \left( 1 - \nu_1^H \right)^\lambda \right] \right), \lambda > 0.$$

