$$\alpha_1 \cup \alpha_2 = \left(\left[\max\left(\mu_1^L, \mu_2^L\right), \max\left(\mu_1^H, \mu_2^H\right)\right], \left[\min\left(\nu_1^L, \nu_2^L\right), \min(\nu_1^H, \nu_2^H)\right]\right);$$

$$\lambda\alpha_1 = \left(\left[1-\left(1-\mu_1^L\right)^\lambda, 1-\left(1-\mu_1^H\right)^\lambda\right], \left[\left(\nu_1^L\right)^\lambda, \left(\nu_1^H\right)^\lambda\right]\right), \quad \lambda > 0;$$

$$\alpha_1^\lambda = \left(\left[\left(\mu_1^L\right)^\lambda, \left(\mu_1^H\right)^\lambda\right], \left[1-\left(1-\nu_1^L\right)^\lambda, 1-\left(1-\nu_1^H\right)^\lambda\right]\right), \quad \lambda > 0;$$

$$\alpha_1^c = \left(\left[\nu_1^L, \nu_1^H\right], \left[\mu_1^L, \mu_1^H\right]\right).$$

**Definition 3** [66]: Let $$A = \left(\left[\mu_A^L, \mu_A^H\right], \left[\nu_A^L, \nu_A^H\right]\right)$$ be an IVIFN, and then its score function $$S(A)$$ is defined as

$$S(A) = \frac{1}{2}\left(\mu_A^L + \mu_A^H + \frac{\mu_A^H + \nu_A^H}{2}\left(1 - \mu_A^L - \nu_A^L\right) + \frac{\mu_A^L + \nu_A^L}{2}\left(1 - \mu_A^H - \nu_A^H\right)\right)$$ (2)

where $$S(A) \in [0, 1]$$.

## III. A NOVEL DIVERGENCE MEASURE FOR IVIFNs

### A. EXISTING DIVERGENCE MEASURES

Wang and Wan [58] gave a standard definition of divergence measures for IVIFSs below.

**Definition 4** [58]: Let X be a finite universe, and let IVIFSs (X) be the set of all IVIFSs on X. A mapping D: IVIFSs (X) × IVIFSs (X) → [0, 1] is a standard divergence measure for IVIFSs if for every A, B ∈ IVIFSs (X) which has the following properties:

(DP1) $$D(A \|B) = 0$$ if and only if $$A = B$$.
(DP2) $$0 \leq D(A \|B) \leq 1$$.
(DP3) $$D(A \|B) = D(B \|A)$$.

First, we review some recent divergence measures for IVIFNs.

Wan and Wang [58]:

$$D_W(A \|B) = \sqrt{\int_0^1 \int_0^1 [p(a \geq b) - p(A \geq B)]^2 d\delta d\beta}$$

where $$a = (\mu_A, \nu_A) = \left(\mu_A^L + \delta\left(\mu_A^H - \mu_A^L\right), \nu_A^L + \beta\left(\nu_A^H - \nu_A^L\right)\right)$$ and $$b = (\mu_B, \nu_B) = \left(\mu_B^L + \delta\left(\mu_B^H - \mu_B^L\right), \nu_B^L + \beta\left(\nu_B^H - \nu_B^L\right)\right)$$ with $$\delta, \beta \in [0, 1]$$,

$$p(a \geq b) = \max\left\{1 - \max\left\{\frac{1 - \nu_B - \mu_A}{2 - \mu_A - \nu_A - \mu_B - \nu_B}, 0\right\}, 0\right\},$$

$$p(A \geq B) = \int_0^1 \int_0^1 p(a \geq b)d\delta d\beta.$$

Li et al. [59]:

$$D_L(A \|B) = \frac{1}{\gamma - 1}\left[\left(\frac{m_A + m_B}{2}\right)^\gamma - \frac{1}{2}\left(m_A^\gamma + m_B^\gamma\right)\right]$$

where $$m_A = \left(\mu_A^L + \mu_A^H + 2 - \nu_A^L - \nu_A^H\right)/4$$, $$m_B = \left(\mu_B^L + \mu_B^H + 2 - \nu_B^L - \nu_B^H\right)/4$$, $$\gamma \in (1, 2]$$.

Mishra et al. [60]:

$$D_{M1}(A \|B)$$

$$= 1 - \log_2\left(1 + \frac{1}{2}\left(\frac{\min\left\{\mu_A^L, \mu_B^L\right\} + \min\left\{\mu_A^H, \mu_B^H\right\} + \min\left\{\nu_A^L, \nu_B^L\right\} + \min\left\{\nu_A^H, \nu_B^H\right\} + \min\left\{\pi_A^L, \pi_B^L\right\} + \min\left\{\pi_A^H, \pi_B^H\right\}}{}\right)\right)$$

$$D_{M2}(A \|B)$$

$$= \begin{cases}
\frac{1}{1-e^{-1/2}}\left|\frac{1}{2}\left(\exp\left(-\left(\frac{\nu_A^L + \nu_A^H + 2 - \mu_A^L - \mu_A^H}{4}\right)\right) + \exp\left(-\left(\frac{\nu_B^L + \nu_B^H + 2 - \mu_B^L - \mu_B^H}{4}\right)\right)\right) - \exp\left(-\frac{1}{8}\left(\frac{\nu_A^L + \nu_A^H + \nu_B^L + \nu_B^H + 4}{-\mu_A^L - \mu_A^H - \mu_B^L - \mu_B^H}\right)\right)\right| & \text{if } \mu_A^L + \mu_A^H \geq \nu_A^L + \nu_A^H \\
\frac{1}{1-e^{-1/2}}\left|\frac{1}{2}\left(\exp\left(-\left(\frac{\mu_A^L + \mu_A^H + 2 - \nu_A^L - \nu_A^H}{4}\right)\right) + \exp\left(-\left(\frac{\mu_B^L + \mu_B^H + 2 - \nu_B^L - \nu_B^H}{4}\right)\right)\right) - \exp\left(-\frac{1}{8}\left(\frac{\mu_A^L + \mu_A^H + \mu_B^L + \mu_B^H + 4}{-\nu_A^L - \nu_A^H - \nu_B^L - \nu_B^H}\right)\right)\right| & \text{if } \mu_A^L + \mu_A^H \prec \nu_A^L + \nu_A^H
\end{cases}$$

Mishra et al. [61]:

$$D_M(A \|B) = \mu_A^L \ln \frac{\mu_A^L}{\left(\mu_A^L + \mu_B^L\right)/2} + \mu_A^H \ln \frac{\mu_A^H}{\left(\mu_A^H + \mu_B^H\right)/2}$$

$$+ \nu_A^L \ln \frac{\nu_A^L}{\left(\nu_A^L + \nu_B^L\right)/2} + \nu_A^H \ln \frac{\nu_A^H}{\left(\nu_A^H + \nu_B^H\right)/2}$$

$$+ \mu_B^L \ln \frac{\mu_B^L}{\left(\mu_A^L + \mu_B^L\right)/2} + \mu_B^H \ln \frac{\mu_B^H}{\left(\mu_A^H + \mu_B^H\right)/2}$$

$$+ \nu_B^L \ln \frac{\nu_B^L}{\left(\nu_A^L + \nu_B^L\right)/2} + \nu_B^H \ln \frac{\nu_B^H}{\left(\nu_A^H + \nu_B^H\right)/2}$$

Now, we advance two examples to illustrate the weaknesses of the above developed divergence measures for IVIFNs. The calculation results are shown in Table 1.

